I am trying to figure out monster magic resistance.  The impetus for
this was trying to figure out what sort of monsters would be good to
hit over the head with a potion of paralysis and which would like
result in wasting the potion.  I was thinking that this would be a
counted as an attack level 6 (potion).  But then I remembered that
Pestilence and Famine, having level 30 and 100 MR, will pass every MR
check, but they can be level drained and then begin to fail MR checks
(vs. taming, for instance).  So the drain life spell is one thing that
doesn't check MR, setting the precedent that maybe paralysis does and
maybe it doesn't check MR.  So is there a list anywhere of what checks
a monster's MR, what checks a monster's resistances, what checks both,
and what check neither?

